# THE FLASH IMAGE IS THE BACKUP. THE REST IS BUILD BY-PRODUCT.
#
# The hard rule on this bench is that the exact image flashed for every run is kept, so any state the
# board has been in can be returned to by flashing one file. That file is the .hex, and it is committed.
#
# arduino-cli also writes a .elf, a .lst, a .sym and a .eep beside it. The .lst alone is 1.6 MB and
# together they are 95% of the archive, and none of them is needed to put the board back -- they are
# regenerated by rebuilding the commit the run.json names. So they stay on disk locally, where they are
# useful for reading disassembly, and out of the history.
*.elf
*.lst
*.sym
*.eep
